<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1030" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχί-μολος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μολεῖν</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>coming near</i>; 
				Ep.
			 word, mostly used in neut. as Adv., <i>near,
				close at hand</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχίμολον δέ οἱ ἦλθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					4.529
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				8.300
			</span></i>, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				325
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἀγχιμόλοιο ἰδών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					24.352
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγχίμολον δὲ μετ᾽ αὐτόν</span>
			<i>close</i> behind him, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				17.336
			</span></i>: c. gen., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕθεν ἀγχίμολοι</span>
			cj. in <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				25.203
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
